  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through Wednesday)\nIssued at 310 PM CDT THU AUG 13 2026\n\nThis afternoon, surface high pressure is present across the\nNorthern Gulf. In the upper levels, a ridge is also centered\nacross the Northern Gulf Coast with weak west northwest flow \nacross Central Alabama. At the surface, little change is expected \nthrough the short term (today through Fri). However, aloft, the \nridge should nudge a little northward. This should help to \nsuppress overall convection a little, and definitely build the \nheat over us. Over this weekend, guidance shows increased \nprobability of an expanding upper ridge over much of Southern \nConus, making isolated diurnal convection by Sun/Mon difficult. In\nthe near term, any storms that do pop up this afternoon and \nevening could grow with gusty winds and brief heavy rainfall.\n\nOutside of any storms, the heat will be the main story. We\ncontinue with a heat advisory for all of Central Alabama for\ntoday through Saturday. There will not be any major features to\nhelp to cool the area off, so look for a high probability of heat\nadvisories to be continued through the weekend. There is a medium\nto high chance that some areas (especially west) could see triple\ndigit high temperatures by Sunday into the beginning of next\nweek.\n\n08",
